.TH START\-MU2EDAQ\-DOWNTIME\-LOGGER.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh \- start the downtime logger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-foreground ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR ARGS ...]
.br
.B start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
The script changes to its own directory, runs
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
if
.I venv/bin/activate
is missing, activates the virtual environment and starts
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1).
.PP
By default the application is started in the background with
.BR nohup ,
standard output and standard error are appended to the log file, and the
child PID is written to
.IR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.pid .
If that PID file names a live process the script refuses to start; a PID
file naming a dead process is removed.
.PP
With
.B \-\-foreground
the script
.BR exec s
the application in place: no PID file is written and output stays on the
terminal.
.PP
.B The default configuration is the workstation test file
.BR config/local.yaml ,
which watches
.I /tmp/daq\-test
and 127.0.0.1:9000/udp and serves the web view on 127.0.0.1:8001.
The control\-room launcher
.B crs\-app
runs this script with no arguments, so it gets that file.
Pass
.B \-\-config
to monitor real DAQ signals.
The script does not read
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
or any other environment variable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
YAML configuration passed to the application.
Default
.IR config/local.yaml .
A relative path is resolved against the package directory, because the
script changes into it first.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
Passed through as
.BR \-\-log\-level :
.BR DEBUG ,
.BR INFO ,
.B WARNING
or
.BR ERROR .
Default
.BR INFO .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " FILE"
Append background output to
.I FILE
instead of
.IR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.log .
Ignored with
.BR \-\-foreground .
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground instead of the background.
.TP
.BI \-\- " ARGS"
Everything after
.B \-\-
is appended to the application command line.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.pid
PID of the background process, in the package directory.
.TP
.I mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.log
Default background log, appended to and never rotated.
.TP
.I venv/
Virtual environment created by
.BR bootstrap.sh (1).
.TP
.I config/local.yaml
Default configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
None read by the script itself.
.B PYTHON
is honoured by
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
when the script has to bootstrap.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The application was started in the background, or
.B \-\-help
was given.
In foreground mode the exit status is that of the application.
.TP
.B 1
Unknown option, an option missing its argument, or a live PID file.
.TP
.B >0
A failing
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
step; the script runs under
.B set \-e
and exits with that step's status.
.PP
A background start returns 0 as soon as the child is forked; a
configuration error in the application is visible only in the log file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start in the background with the workstation test configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start against a site configuration with a dedicated log file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh \e
    \-\-config /path/to/site.yaml \e
    \-\-log\-file /var/log/mu2edaq/downtime\-logger.log
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run in the foreground with debug logging:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh \-\-foreground \-\-log\-level DEBUG
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.yaml (5)
